{
    "attributes": {
        "action": "Allow all legal residents paying tax in England & Northern Ireland to vote",
        "additional_details": "We believe \u201ctaxation without representation\u201d is wrong in principle: people who pay taxes and are affected by decisions should be able to vote to shape national decisions. \u201cLawful residents\u201d means people who are legally entitled to reside in the UK and who can obtain government-issued identification (e.g., a NI number, a driving licence, or similar).",
        "background": "We call on the UK Government to amend electoral law and extend voting rights in all general and local elections in England and Northern Ireland to anyone who is legally residing there and paying tax.",
